    31	There was a dray in the lane. It was a long low thing on four wheels, with two brown cobs in its shafts, and it was loaded to the rails with coils, tarred and white, under a sheet that had not yet been lashed down. A lean man with a straw in his mouth was going round it, trying each knot.
