   191	*Two hundred and ninety-sixth day. The halting-ground in the fold; thirteen miles. The cut walked east. Water in it, and no glass, and sheep on the top. Vastin walked it: seventeen of thirty. He stood on the leg once, with the stick off the ground, where the line had been. The factor offered twenty at each first frost, and a seat for the old man at the hold's fire. Brom said no. A hundred and twenty-eight.*
