    29	The Force went out along a line and was done. He had been paid for that for the better part of his life, and it had made him first on a sheet of sailcloth: he could put his palm to a thing that six men could not shift, and it shifted. It was a thing for roads: a block came down on a ledge, or a wheel went into a ditch, or a gate would not open; and he arrived, and it was settled, and the wrist kept the account.
    30	
    31	A wall did not arrive. It stayed. It could not come to the trouble; the trouble had to be brought to it, and whoever stood behind it had to be worth the bringing. He had seen that much from a factor's telling; the boy with the book had seen it from two feet away, and had gone and stood there.
    32	
