   108	| **NEW — The shale-back herd at the axe-head fence** (cold weather) [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] | summarized as "we walked the fence" | 3,000 | A cold-weather set piece [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] needing no Path: a herd of armoured grazers sheltering on the fence line's slope must be moved without stampeding them ("lethal on a slope when herded wrong"). It teaches the Iron read on frozen ground, Lira benched by her sling, Seln's posts, and Brom reading a line. |
   109	| **NEW — The ice road** (161st) | one line | 3,000 | A carter's cart goes through the river-ice. Cael, Brom and Seln haul it out without declaring, reading load on the ice. The fragments are taught as practical knowledge. It pays later at the cut's frozen runnel. |
   110	| **NEW — The silent yard** (cold-weather learning bouts with Teague's crew) [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 6] | absent | 3 bouts × ~1,500 = 4,500 | No Paths, steel and bodies only, in the frozen meadow. Cael loses to the tall man [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: M1 audit; OWNER-pending #59]'s spear reach (she never speaks), then corrects. One-armed Lira coaches from the bench. The rival clock appears on the page. This must not touch the sequence locks in §13 (no wall drill; Seln teaches nobody). |
