   155	### E. New episodes inside canon (≈23,000; most are counted under A above)
   156	
   157	The shale-back fence, the ice road, the silent yard, Lira's return to the floor, the ferry landing, the tail in Treswick, and the water at the seep (see A). Also Oryn's north circuit (cutaways only): Oxhollow's gate, a man with a wrist set wrong, a birth, and **a hold child's Kindling**, where Oryn watches a fourteen-year-old see a sigil nobody else can see. No patient dies under her hands (§13).
   158	
   159	### F. Humour and warmth (≈12,000, distributed; no quota)
   160	
   161	Each person keeps their own comic habit. Brom says "It's a boot" and gives one-word essays ("They shoe by the tier"). Pike speaks ledger. Oryn: "Everybody says that now" and "I'm going to have to find another word". Lira finds an essay in a single word. "Noted" spreads through the cast like a borrowed tool, in the sequence locked in §13. Running jokes: the mule's empty chair; the mule as the only one of twelve who never knows what happened; the ferryman watching people use his river; Vastin's good manners from a man "served all his life and never once fed". When pain is in the room, humour stops performing.
