   285	### 7.3 Development cadence (owner formula §5)
   286	
   287	- **Cael:** about 4.5 realization/decision beats per 10k words, ≈135 across the book, spread evenly with a slight middle bump (≈42 / 48 / 45). That is about 15 per movement, so roughly one every 2,200 words.
   288	- **Supporting cast:** many small beats each (§3.D), 0.1–0.7 per 10k per person. No single deuteragonist takes the budget. Karis and Vastin run highest (≈14 each across the book); Pike and the young one run lowest.
   289	
   290	### 7.4 Prose and rhythm targets (formula §2–3, §8–9; measured after each movement with `tools/formula_metrics.py`)
   291	
   292	**Source baseline** (measured 2026-10-01 over all 24 chapters):
   293	
   294	| Metric | Source | Target |
   295	|---|---|---|
   296	| Sentence mean | 21.3 | 14.6 |
   297	| Sentence median | 8 | 11 |
   298	| Spread (sd) | 27.2 | ~26 |
   299	| Sentences ≤5 words | 39.3% | 27.7% |
   300	| Sentences ≥40 words | **19.1%** | 3.3% |
   301	| Paragraph median | **51** | ~18 |
   302	| Paragraph mean | 66.4 | ~26.8 |
   303	| Words per scene | 808 | ~950 |
   304	| Scene breaks per 10k | 10.0 | ~8.7 |
   305	| Flesch Reading Ease | 85.0 | 72.3 |
   306	| FK grade | 6.7 | 6.8 |
   307	
   308	The source's signature is the accumulating catalogue sentence, chained with "and … and … because …". That produces both the 19% of sentences over forty words and the paragraphs of fifty-plus words, while very short beats pull the median and the Flesch score up. **For this edition:**
   309	- Break the catalogue chains into well-built compound and complex sentences of 12–25 words.
   310	- Keep a few deliberate forty-plus sentences per chapter where accumulation is the effect, such as an inventory or a crossing.
   311	- Bring paragraphs down toward a median of 18 by ending the paragraph when the thought turns.
   312	- Keep short punch sentences for landings, not as default (EDITION_BRIEF rhythm calibration).
   313	- Hold a scene break roughly every 950 words.
   314	- Drop dialogue tags where the speaker is clear.
   315	- Adverbs and fillers are to taste: do not chase "that".
   316	
   317	**Logs are exempt from the chain-breaking only where §10 fixes their text.**
