   331	## 9. The record passages: exact limits
   332	
   333	- **The leaf is read aloud once**, by Karis, in the chamber, on the 293rd morning (M6). It is not quoted again by anyone who heard it. Cael gives Lira the page to read; nobody says it back.
   334	- **"Four hundred years"** appears only in the record's voice (the leaf's head, given in Karis's single paraphrase) and at the fixed positions: Cael's pole-two sentence, the 298th log, the 305th close dialogue and the closing prose. Do not add uses.
   335	- **"The Architect"** is the record's **title** ("a title, not a name; the name's gone"). After the leaf it appears again only as a historical comparison ("as old as the Architect"). Nobody uses it as a present agent.
   336	- **The chronicle's hole stays a hole.** "Marked." There is no gloss, guess or second source.
   337	- **The un-bound / [UNBOUND]:** the word is live as a historical *kind* in the leaf. Before that, Karis uses it once as a stratum limit ("Older than [UNBOUND]") at Cleon's table.
   338	- **Two pages, no line.** The leaf and the lamps finding are never joined: not in dialogue, not in any interior (including cutaways), not in the narration. Vastin's sentence stops twice (in the chamber; on the shale). The words *terminal*, *circuit* and *infrastructure* are never used for Arbiters.
   339	- **The deep-layer sheet:** "Sequence initiated … Correlated with classification event —" and the bar. Only Cael and Seln do the sum. Neither says or writes it. Nobody interprets the sequence.
