   408	- **S21:** "Behind it. Noted?" / "Noted," (the young one). The far-mouth realization: the line "was not ink".
   409	- **S22 log body:** "Turned the Rune fragment on myself. Cleon said don't. The reading only ever told me the still place was nothing — no flow, no current, a hole where a man should have a middle. The Rune sense says it's not a hole. It says it's *built like something* — like one of those floors with nothing standing on it. Same shape to that fragment as the sites are to Cleon's. I'm not going to write what that might mean, because I don't know, and because the last time I wrote something true in this log a healer made me swear an oath about it. The instruments read wronger for me than they did at Lowmarch. The trend's climbing. My Arbiter's still dark—nothing in me to go quiet, same as always. Tomorrow, the oldest one. I've spent the whole year wanting to stand in the middle of it. I think part of me already knows what I'm going to feel. Nothing. I think I'm going to feel nothing, and I think that's going to be the loudest thing that's ever happened to me." [OWNER-pending #58] ("the whole year", never "the whole book".) [OWNER-pending #58]
   410	- **S23 close:** "Every other one, yours worked and ours died." / "Yes." / "You think this one's different." / "I think this one's the first one they made," … "I think if any place on the continent is going to tell me what I am, it's the one they built to make sure I'd never be." / He stepped over the line. / His Path did not die. It also did not *notice* it should have. [OWNER-pending #57] / "Wait here," he said, and did not look back, and walked toward the center of the oldest quiet, alone.
   411	- **S24 ledger:** "Thirteen: Wind, Pressure, Iron, Compression, Ember, Shadow, Storm, Anchor, Blade, Tide, Iron Wall, Rune, Force. One anomaly, the still place, read by two instruments — the tenth, which says nothing, and the twelfth, which says a shape — and understood by neither. Not the Quiet. Not a fragment. The same kind of made. That is as far as the instruments go and I am not going past them." / "Stood in the middle of the first one. Nothing. Entered." **The letter:** "Nineteen. Your grandmother's line was already drawn. I followed it to the end; both edges agreed. Tell Lira's family I said so. Mind the shape, you said. I'm minding it. — C." [OWNER-pending #55] (§12 C11.) Lira: "Well?" / "I'll tell you on the road," … "If there's road."
   412	- **Closing prose (S24):** "He had spent the whole year learning that the world was built to prevent him — four hundred years of tiers and registries and a machine that lit for everyone but him, all of it laid down so that what he was would never come again. And at the center of the first place they ever made, the oldest silence on the continent, the one built before there was a word for it, he had felt no exclusion and no prevention and no wall. He had felt at home. He did not have a word for that yet. But he knew, now, walking back out across a floor older than the system that had expelled him, that it was not an accident — that the place built to end him was the one place he fit — and that the difference between *the system was built to exclude me* and *the system was built to prevent me* had a third sentence past it, waiting, that he was not ready to write. Someone had made the pattern. He was, he was beginning to understand, the pattern. That was as far as he could say." [OWNER-pending #57] [OWNER-pending #58]
